{"name":"Lap Dog","hex":"#a6927f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lap dog","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small toy dog, kept as household pet, whose light weight and companionable temperament make it both suited and disposed to spend time resting in the comfort of its master's lap; a dog bred to behave in this manner.","A person who behaves in a servile manner, such as a sycophantic employee or a fawning lover."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lap_dog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lap dog","blocks":[{"text":"A lap dog or lapdog is a dog that is both small enough to be held in the arms or lie comfortably on a person's lap and temperamentally predisposed to doing so. Lapdog is not a specific breed, but a generic term for a type of dog that is small in size and friendly toward humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Louis-Michel_van_Loo_Princess_Ekaterina_Dmitrievna_Golitsyna.jpg/330px-Louis-Michel_van_Loo_Princess_Ekaterina_Dmitrievna_Golitsyna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lap_dog","wikidata":"Q38914"},{"title":"Lap","blocks":[{"text":"A lap is a surface created between the knee and hips of a biped when it is in a seated or lying down position. The lap of a parent or loved one is seen as a physically and psychologically comfortable place for a child to sit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/%27In_slaap_gesust%27_Rijksmuseum_SK-A-2378.jpeg/330px-%27In_slaap_gesust%27_Rijksmuseum_SK-A-2378.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lap","wikidata":"Q1276686"},{"title":"Dog","blocks":[{"text":"The dog is a domesticated descendant of wolves. Also called the domestic dog, it was selectively bred during the Late Pleistocene by hunter-gatherers. Dogs and the modern gray wolf share a common ancestor. Dogs were the first species to be domesticated over 14,000 years ago, before the development of agriculture, though genetic studies suggest the domestication process may have begun over 25,000 years ago. Due to their long association with humans, dogs have gained the ability to thrive on a starch-rich diet that would be inadequate for other canids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Huskiesatrest.jpg/330px-Huskiesatrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog","wikidata":"Q144"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Chou_Fang_003.jpg/500px-Chou_Fang_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Chou_Fang_003.jpg/500px-Chou_Fang_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two women playing with a lap dog, China, 8th century, Beauties Wearing Flowers by Tang dynasty painter Zhou Fang","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChou_Fang_003.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Christophe_Huet_Portrait_of_Mimi%2C_Madame_De_Pompadour%27s_King_Charles_Spaniel%2C_In_a_Landscape.jpg/500px-Christophe_Huet_Portrait_of_Mimi%2C_Madame_De_Pompadour%27s_King_Charles_Spaniel%2C_In_a_Landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Christophe_Huet_Portrait_of_Mimi%2C_Madame_De_Pompadour%27s_King_Charles_Spaniel%2C_In_a_Landscape.jpg/1280px-Christophe_Huet_Portrait_of_Mimi%2C_Madame_De_Pompadour%27s_King_Charles_Spaniel%2C_In_a_Landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Christophe_Huet_Portrait_of_Mimi%2C_Madame_De_Pompadour%27s_King_Charles_Spaniel%2C_In_a_Land